        // The general rule: for every admissible input, when reference completes it returns true.
        // We assert that whenever the call did not revert, its return is true.
        // Because the reference C always returns true (when not reverted), this must hold for all inputs.
        // The mutant that returns the first call's success can return false here (first call to reverter fails),
        // so this assertion will fail on the mutant for some inputs.
        // Single assertion required by the harness:
        if (okRef) {
            assertTrue(okRef);
